      "body": "## Motivation\n\nInput logprob assembly currently replaces token ID `vocab_size - 1` with `0`, even though valid IDs are in `[0, vocab_size)`. This can attach an input logprob to the wrong token in the response.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Preserve all IDs below `vocab_size`; continue replacing multimodal placeholder IDs at or above that boundary with `0`.\n- Extend the existing registered CPU test with the maximum valid ID and exact/above-vocabulary placeholders, covering nested/flat output and one-shot/chunked prefill. Also check that logprob values and original request IDs are preserved.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n```bash\npython test/registered/unit/managers/test_flat_raw_top_logprobs.py -v\n```\n\nLinux, Python 3.12, Torch 2.11: all 36 tests pass. The unchanged production source with the same tests fails the four new subcases; all other cases pass. Both arms use complete source and the test's existing CPU optional-kernel fixture. No server, model weights or GPU workload was used; the official CPU CI/dependency matrix remains pending.\n\nFocused isort, Ruff, formatting, codespell and basic pre-commit checks pass on both changed files. Please run `base-a-test-cpu` when convenient.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable: this fixes returned token metadata, not model computation or a performance path.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format the changed code.\n- [x] Add focused regression coverage.\n- [ ] Documentation changes — not applicable.\n- [ ] Model accuracy/speed benchmarks — not applicable.\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style guidance.\n\nDeveloped and validated with assistance from OpenAI Codex.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38628705089](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38628705089)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38628705071](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38628705071)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38628705003](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38628705003)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
